(A program that never committed to file I/O was never given a path, and
 one that was given no stdin must not read it, so the path-building leaves
 and the stdin leaf stand aside for the plain-print leaf instead.)
Print "--- the path and stdin leaves with no file I/O and no stdin committed ---".
Set gen_does_file_io to false.
Set gen_reads_stdin to false.
'rng seed' of 1.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf file properties worked example' of "" and false.
Print "emits a file open: {'gen text contains' of \"open a file\"}".
'rng seed' of 1.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf file appending rounds' of "" and false.
Print "emits a file open: {'gen text contains' of \"open a file\"}".
'rng seed' of 1.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf file writing truncates' of "" and false.
Print "emits a file open: {'gen text contains' of \"open a file\"}".
'rng seed' of 1.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf read line through a file' of "" and false.
Print "emits a file open: {'gen text contains' of \"open a file\"}".
'rng seed' of 1.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf standard input read' of "" and false.
Print "reads standard input: {'gen text contains' of \"standard input\"}".
(The borrowed-descriptor leaf builds no path, so it still runs - but
 with no stdin committed it must never borrow descriptor 0.)
'rng seed' of 7.
'gen buffer names reset'.
clear gen_out.
'gen leaf file borrowed descriptors' of "" and false.
Print "borrows descriptor 0: {'gen text contains' of \"at 0\"}".
Set gen_does_file_io to true.
Set gen_reads_stdin to true.
